<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml" xmlns:h="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" version="1.0" name="Selection" initial="inactive"><metadata><h:section id="documentation"><h:h2>Selection — actor contract</h:h2><h:p><h:strong>Actor invariant: </h:strong>Owned DOM references are transient; locator record and hashes are durable.</h:p><h:p><h:strong>Specification: </h:strong>ACT-SELECTION in <h:a href="../system.xml">system.xml</h:a>. These comments use XHTML namespace h: and are not executable SCXML actions.</h:p><h:h3>I/O contracts invoked by this actor</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-DOM-HOVER">review.dom.hover</h:a> — HoverRequest → HoverResult | Fault; read, never, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-004, FL-028; requirements: REQ-013, REQ-025</h:li><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-DOM-ANCHOR">review.dom.anchor</h:a> — AnchorRequest → AnchorResult | Fault; read, never, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-004, FL-005, FL-013; requirements: REQ-013, REQ-014, REQ-016</h:li><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-DOM-REGION">review.dom.region</h:a> — RegionRequest → RegionResult | Fault; read, never, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-009; requirements: REQ-015, REQ-023</h:li><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-DOM-INSPECT">review.dom.inspect</h:a> — PageInspectRequest → PageInspectResult | Fault; read, never, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-004, FL-008, FL-035; requirements: REQ-013, REQ-021, REQ-071</h:li></h:ul></h:section></metadata><state id="inactive">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-inactive"><h:h3>State: inactive</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>selection.hover</h:code> → hovering</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="selection.hover" target="hovering"/>
  </state>
  <state id="hovering">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-hovering"><h:h3>State: hovering</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>selection.anchor</h:code> → anchored</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="selection.anchor" target="anchored"/>
  </state>
  <state id="anchored">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-anchored"><h:h3>State: anchored</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>selection.region</h:code> → region</h:li><h:li><h:code>patch.invalidated</h:code> → stale</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="selection.region" target="region"/>
    <transition event="patch.invalidated" target="stale"/>
  </state>
  <state id="region"><metadata><h:section id="state-region"><h:h3>State: region</h:h3><h:p>No outgoing transitions in this version. This state is terminal until the host ends or restores the actor.</h:p></h:section></metadata></state>
  <state id="stale">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-stale"><h:h3>State: stale</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>selection.anchor</h:code> → anchored</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="selection.anchor" target="anchored"/>
  </state>
</scxml>
